            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "587cdba4-cefb-4df9-8514-2e50ccf88739",
               "text": "Penzias, A. A., & Wilson, R. W.",
               "page": "https://doi.org/10.1086/148307",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "1965",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Sharing with Nobody\n\nIn the first moments of the universe, everything was together, but nothing had the shape we observe today. There were no stars, no planets, and no galaxies: it was a single, extremely hot and dense state.\n\nSince there was no one to receive and nothing separated to share, let us look at the image below to remember that first state.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img src=\"https://www.historytracers.org/images/ESA/Planck_history_of_Universe.jpg\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 1</b>: Planck history of the Universe. ESA - C. Carreau.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "070951b5-5b4c-4622-9380-ad81313f6564",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "070951b5-5b4c-4622-9380-ad81313f6564",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Let Us Think!\n\nIn the first moments of the universe, everything was concentrated in a single point, and there was nobody and nothing else to receive it.\n\n**Is it possible to share (to divide) something when there is nobody and nothing to receive it?**",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "9163665b-ce43-486d-a897-0f7222aecbf2",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "no",
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "9163665b-ce43-486d-a897-0f7222aecbf2",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "58da6d75-ce8a-45f5-b57f-1f0763ee3568",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=58da6d75-ce8a-45f5-b57f-1f0763ee3568",
               "date_time": {
