            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "6dfe4b3b-8338-46ab-8149-2e073414907e",
               "text": "NASA",
               "page": "https://science.nasa.gov/universe/overview/",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### A More Complex Scenario\n\nThe initial universe is even more complex. Since nothing had been created yet and nothing was separated, the universe could not share anything at that time.\n\nOn the next screen, we will observe that, even today, we also have situations where it is not possible to share.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "f2c64edb-48ba-4c2b-8ec3-34bc421eae27",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "f2c64edb-48ba-4c2b-8ec3-34bc421eae27",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "shocking",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "58da6d75-ce8a-45f5-b57f-1f0763ee3568",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=58da6d75-ce8a-45f5-b57f-1f0763ee3568",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "fc6c2a04-8a51-4ea5-847d-9b71912828ea",
               "text": "Weisstein, Eric W.",
               "page": "https://mathworld.wolfram.com/DivisionbyZero.html",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### The Empty Region\n\nLook at the table below. On its left side, there are two circles. Imagine that we want to share (to divide) one circle with a person on the right side. However, there is nobody on the right side: it is an empty region.\n\nNo matter how many circles we place on the left, there is no one to receive them on the right. Without a receiver, the sharing cannot happen.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table class=\"book_navigation\"><tr><td>Left side</td><td>Right side</td></tr><tr><td><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:3em;height:3em;border-radius:50%;background-color:#1B4F72;margin-right:0.5em;\"></span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:3em;height:3em;border-radius:50%;background-color:#1B4F72;margin-right:0.5em;\"></span></td><td style=\"min-width:6em;border:1px dashed #999999;\">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><b>Table 1</b>: Two circles on the left and an empty region on the right. There is no one to receive the shared circle.</td></tr></table></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
