                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nIn this class, we remembered that the initial state of the universe had everything concentrated, with nothing separated yet.\n\nWe also observed that we cannot share (divide) something with others when there is no one else to receive it: sharing always needs at least one receiver.\n\nTherefore, we cannot define a division by zero. Division by zero is **undefined**.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
